{
  "id": "27901_touseki",
  "headword": "透析",
  "reading": "とうせき",
  "romaji": "touseki",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "dialysis",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "dialysis (kidney treatment)",
      "explanation": "A medical treatment that filters waste and excess fluid from the blood when the kidneys can no longer do so. Usually refers to {人工透析|じんこうとうせき} (artificial dialysis)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27901_touseki_ex1",
      "japanese": "{週|しゅう}に{三回|さんかい}{透析|とうせき}を{受|う}ける。",
      "english": "He gets dialysis three times a week.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27901_touseki_ex2",
      "japanese": "{腎臓|じんぞう}の{機能|きのう}が{低下|ていか}し、{透析|とうせき}が{必要|ひつよう}になった。",
      "english": "His kidney function declined, and he came to need dialysis.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27901_touseki_ex3",
      "japanese": "{透析|とうせき}{患者|かんじゃ}は{食事|しょくじ}や{水分|すいぶん}の{管理|かんり}に{気|き}を{付|つ}ける{必要|ひつよう}がある。",
      "english": "Dialysis patients need to be careful about managing their diet and fluid intake.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Can take する: {透析|とうせき}する (to undergo / perform dialysis).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {透析|とうせき}を{受|う}ける: to undergo dialysis\n- {人工透析|じんこうとうせき}: artificial dialysis\n- {透析|とうせき}{患者|かんじゃ}: dialysis patient\n- {透析|とうせき}{治療|ちりょう}: dialysis treatment",
